namespace NK.CFTLib.ArtinReciprocityIdeal

/-- **The index of the product of the principal ray and the norm group is at most the degree.**

This is the `≤` direction of Milne, *Class Field Theory*, Chapter VI, Theorem 4.9
(`(I^{S(m)} : i(K_{m,1})·N_m(I_L^{S(m)})) ≤ [L : K]`), in the ideal-theoretic vocabulary of
`LangDefs.lean`: the subgroup of the ideals coprime to `(m)` generated by the principal ideals
`(a)` with `a ≡ 1 mod (m)` totally positive and by the relative norms of ideals of `L` coprime to
`(m)` has index at most `[L : K]`.

The proof reduces the ideal-theoretic index to the idèle-theoretic norm index
`(NK.GlobalCFT.Idele.normClassSubgroup K L).index` — this is the idèle–ideal dictionary
(Milne, Proposition 4.6, together with the identification of the norm groups), established in
`indexIdealCoprimeLeNormClassIndex` — and then invokes the (unconditional) second inequality
`NK.GlobalCFTdeep.index_le_finrank_of_isGalois`

    `(normClassSubgroup K L).index ≤ Module.finrank K L`.

Since `Subgroup.index` is *defined* as `Nat.card (G ⧸ H)`, the first step is a rewriting. -/
theorem indexPrincipalRaySupNormRayLe (K L : Type) [Field K] [NumberField K] [Field L]
    [NumberField L] [Algebra K L] [FiniteDimensional K L] [IsGalois K L] (m : ℕ) (hm : 0 < m) :
    ((NK.CFTLib.ArtinReciprocityIdeal.principalRay K m ⊔
        NK.CFTLib.ArtinReciprocityIdeal.normRay K L m).subgroupOf
      (NK.CFTLib.ArtinReciprocityIdeal.idealCoprimeGroup K m)).index ≤ Module.finrank K L := by
  refine le_trans ?_ (NK.GlobalCFTdeep.index_le_finrank_of_isGalois (K := K) (L := L))
  exact indexIdealCoprimeLeNormClassIndex K L m hm

end NK.CFTLib.ArtinReciprocityIdeal
